 succeeded in 2266ms:
   1: ---
   2: name: local-pitfall-memory
   3: description: |
   4:   Local pitfall memory for build/runtime errors: before guessing a fix, look up whether THIS machine has seen and VERIFIED a fix for the same error before; after a fix is verified, commit it into the local knowledge base (本地踩坑记忆库：报错先查本机历史，修复验证后沉淀入库，历史与检索永不出机). Use this skill when the user or the agent, in Chinese or English, hits a terminal/build/runtime error and asks 这个报错见过吗/以前怎么修的/查一下踩坑库/记录这次修复/生成踩坑文档, or "have we seen this error", "look up pitfall", "log this fix", "digest pitfalls". Trigger on Chinese verbs like 查坑/记坑/沉淀/归因/踩坑 and English verbs like lookup/log/commit/digest pitfall, and explicit mentions of 报错/exception/traceback/error/stderr/本地/离线/offline/AIPC.
   5: 
   6:   Supported inputs/categories:
   7:   - Raw error text: compiler errors, stack traces, npm/pip/cargo failures, HTTP errors, exit codes
   8:   - Fix records: the command or change that fixed an error, plus how it was verified
   9:   - Digest requests: compile the local database into a Markdown pitfalls table
  10: 
  11:   Prefer this skill over re-deriving a fix from scratch whenever the error may have occurred on this machine before — a verified historical fix beats a fresh guess.
  12: ---
  13: 
  14: # Local Pitfall Memory Skill Guide
  15: 
  16: 给 Agent 装一块长在本机、只记住已验证修复的踩坑记忆：历史库与检索不出机，同一个坑不再从头猜。
  17: 
  18: ## Usage
  19: 
  20: ### Look up an error (查坑)
  21: 
  22: ```
  23: scripts\run.ps1 lookup --request-file request.json --json
  24: ```
  25: 
  26: `request.json`: `{"error_text": "<full error output>", "context": {"cwd": "...", "runtime": "node|python|..."}}`
  27: 
  28: Returns a match card: `{"hit": "exact|family|semantic|none", "confidence": "可引用|需谨慎|仅联想", "resolution": {...}, "verified": true}`.
  29: 
  30: ### Propose a fix record (预沉淀，未验证)
  31: 
  32: ```
  33: scripts\run.ps1 propose --request-file fix.json --json
  34: ```
  35: 
  36: ### Commit after verification (验证通过才入库高置信档)
  37: 
  38: ```
  39: scripts\run.ps1 commit --id <proposal-id> --verify-exit-code 0 --json
  40: ```
  41: 
  42: ### Digest the knowledge base (汇编踩坑文档)
  43: 
  44: ```
  45: scripts\run.ps1 digest --out pitfalls.md
  46: ```
  47: 
  48: ### Health check
  49: 
  50: ```
  51: scripts\run.ps1 status --json
  52: ```
  53: 
  54: Important:
  55: - `scripts\run.ps1` is the only supported interface — do not call other scripts directly.
  56: - Multi-line error text MUST go through `--request-file`, never inline shell quotes.
  57: - First call downloads the local model; if it times out, run `scripts\run.ps1 --continue` to resume.
  58: - Never fall back to a cloud service; the database and all retrieval stay on this machine.
  59: - Only `commit`-ed (verified) resolutions can be returned as 可引用; un-verified proposals surface as 需谨慎 at best.
  60: 
  61: ### Interpreting the reply
  62: 
  63: - 命中层级: exact（指纹全同）/ family（同类错误）/ semantic（语义相近）/ none
  64: - 置信标签: 可引用（已验证+环境兼容）/ 需谨慎（未验证或环境有差）/ 仅联想（仅语义相似）
  65: - 修复卡: 根因 / 修复命令 / 验证方式 / 上次命中时间与次数
  66: 
  67: ## What this skill does NOT do
  68: 
  69: - It does not fix bugs itself and does not replace the agent's own reasoning — it only serves this machine's verified history.
  70: - It does not send error text, code, or history anywhere off this machine.

